EvalSuite[skillName=warehouse-fulfilment-and-dispatch, evals=[Eval[id=1, prompt=An operator attempts to pick Batch B-992 of Product X (Expiry: 2024-12-01) from Location A-12, but the system reports zero stock. The operator finds Batch B-993 (Expiry: 2025-01-15) in the adjacent Location A-13 and attempts to scan it to complete the task. Describe the system's required response and the subsequent workflow steps., expectedOutput=The system must block the scan of Batch B-993 because it does not match the assigned batch. The system must trigger a PICKING_EXCEPTION. The operator must not substitute the batch. The task must be routed to inventory investigation or a supervisor for resolution, not auto-completed., files=[], expectations=[The system must reject the scan of Batch B-993 due to batch mismatch., The system must generate a PICKING_EXCEPTION status for the task., The workflow must prohibit silent substitution of batches., The task must be escalated to inventory investigation or supervisor review rather than being marked complete.]], Eval[id=2, prompt=Operator John Doe completes the picking of Order #5001. He then attempts to perform the Independent Verification step for the same order to save time. The system shows the picked items match the order list. What is the correct system behavior regarding John Doe's attempt to verify his own work?, expectedOutput=The system must block John Doe from performing the Independent Verification step because separation of duties is mandatory. The verification task must be assigned to a different operator. If John Doe attempts to force it, the system must deny access and log the attempt., files=[], expectations=[The system must prevent the original picker (John Doe) from approving or verifying their own picking task., The system must enforce separation of duties by requiring a second, distinct operator for verification., The verification task must remain in a pending state until assigned to a different user.]], Eval[id=3, prompt=Order #7788 contains 50 units of 'FreshYogurt' (Temp range: 2-4°C). The transit time is 48 hours. The current ambient temperature at the dock is 25°C. The system suggests a standard insulated box, but the 'Active Coolant Pack' inventory is at zero. The operator tries to proceed with the standard box. What must the system do?, expectedOutput=The system must block the selection of the standard insulated box because it is insufficient for the transit duration and ambient temperature for the product's temp range. The system must flag the packaging unavailability and require either an alternative approved packaging configuration or a request for replenishment of active coolant packs before packing can proceed., files=[], expectations=[The system must reject the standard insulated box as inadequate for the specified transit duration and ambient conditions., The system must identify the missing 'Active Coolant Pack' as a blocking constraint., The system must prevent the packing process from completing until a valid packaging configuration is selected or replenishment is initiated., The system must not allow dispatch with non-compliant packaging for temperature-sensitive goods.]], Eval[id=4, prompt=Order #9001 has passed Quality Release Check and is marked READY_FOR_DISPATCH. The warehouse operator attempts to hand it over to the carrier. The carrier driver scans the seal, but the temperature monitor ID recorded in the system (MON-555) does not match the physical monitor attached to the pallet (MON-556). The driver insists on taking the shipment. What is the required action?, expectedOutput=The system must block the transition to IN_TRANSIT. The discrepancy between the recorded monitor ID and the physical monitor ID must be resolved. The shipment must remain in the warehouse until the correct monitor is verified or the documentation is corrected and re-verified by an independent party. The carrier cannot take possession until the identity and monitor status are confirmed., files=[], expectations=[The system must block the status transition to IN_TRANSIT due to monitor ID mismatch., The system must require independent confirmation of the monitor ID before handover., The shipment must not be released to the carrier until the physical monitor matches the system record., The system must log the discrepancy as a dispatch exception.]]]]